# API Client and Auth Rules

- Route API calls through `~/lib/api/api-client.ts` `fetcher`.
- Auth API base: `VITE_API_BASE_URL` (default `http://localhost:3010/api/v1`).
- Use `credentials: "include"` for cookie-based session (BFF model per ADR-002).
- Avoid ad-hoc raw `fetch` for internal API endpoints (except `fetchAbsolute` for `/health`).
- Use `authApi` / `accountApi` modules — do not duplicate endpoint strings in routes.

## CSRF (double-submit)

Backend sets `user-xsrf-token` (non-httpOnly) on login. State-changing requests (`POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`) must send:

- Cookie: `user-xsrf-token`
- Header: `X-XSRF-TOKEN` (same value)

`fetcher` attaches the header automatically when the cookie is present. Do not read JWTs in client JS — session cookies are httpOnly.

## SSR cookie propagation

On the server, `fetcher` forwards the incoming `Cookie` header to the API and appends `Set-Cookie` from API responses to the SolidStart response via `vinxi/http`. Login/register/logout actions must run as `"use server"` functions so cookies reach the browser.

## Session

- `getSession` / `useSession` — `authApi.checkAuth()` wrapped in a router query (`user-session`).
- Protected routes use `(protected)` layout; auth pages use `(auth)` layout.
- Auto-refresh on `401`: `fetcher` calls `POST /auth/refresh` once, then retries (refresh token rotation on backend).

## Cookie names (user)

| Cookie | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `userAccessToken` | httpOnly access JWT |
| `userRefreshToken` | httpOnly refresh JWT |
| `user-xsrf-token` | CSRF token (readable by JS for header) |

Separate from admin console cookies on the same API origin.
